WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
All of us are trying to get through this

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.440
the best that we can

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.570
and we're finding
ourselves making decisions

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.030
we might not make otherwise.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.390
I understand that you've fostering a dog.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.340
You've been taking care of a
dog temporarily, is that true?

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.080
Oh my god, what's his name?

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.070
Yes, this is Tommy.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.830
This is Tommy, he's a
little old man. (laughs)

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.670
But he is the sweetest dog ever.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.410
You know, I'm home all the time now.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.780
Usually I'm working and traveling,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.260
and I can't take care of dog.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.730
But, yeah, I had a friend reach out.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.880
I was not planning on
having a dog that day

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.550
and then the next thing
I know I got this guy.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.123
So if you go to @wagmor,

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.470
if anybody's interested
in adopting little Tommy,

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.640
I'm gonna have until he
finds a forever home.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:47.510
But, I mean, look at this.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.670
Look at this face!

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.200
Oh, look at that guy!
(Evan laughs)

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.033
You know what, I have to say,

00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.887
he doesn't look thrilled to be seeing me.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.910
(Evan laughs)

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.740
His face kind of fell like, "oh, that one.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.430
That host, huh, all right, okay."

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.060
So, I wanna get the word out,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.910
because if someone's out there

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:08.270
who would love a sweet, older...

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.000
Let's just say mature dog.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:10.950
A mature dog.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.140
He's mature, yes.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.440
And it's @wagmor?

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:19.853
Mm-hmm, wagmor, just M-O-R, yeah.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.900
Yeah, he's a sweetie and
he's very low maintenance.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:26.140
He doesn't do a whole lot now,

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.550
except just wanna be
cuddled, and fed, and yeah.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.090
So if anybody wants
little Tommy, he's here.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.340
Yeah, I'm telling you,

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.960
as someone who's quite
a bit older than you,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.311
that happens later on.

00:01:35.311 --> 00:01:36.144
Yeah (laughs).

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.203
I wanna be cuddled, I wanna be held,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.550
occasionally dragged onto the porch

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:44.470
to take care of whatever
I have to take care of,

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.107
and then dragged back in again.

00:01:46.107 --> 00:01:47.610
That's exactly right.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.060
That's pretty much my life.

